{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_port_philosophy", "label": "Port Philosophy (port-with-tests, no algorithm changes)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A module is ported when its POC tests pass unmodified; port \u2192 verify \u2192 improve later as a separate change, because improving during the port makes every diff ambiguous between defect and enhancement."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_domaincontext", "label": "DomainContext (rules + catalog + projection)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_rulescontext", "label": "RulesContext (injected market rules)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_catalogcontext", "label": "CatalogContext (two-tier catalog envelope)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_projectioncontext", "label": "ProjectionContext (equirect default, UTM/ENU alongside)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Introduced at port time because every coordinate consumer is being touched anyway; the default implementation is the existing equirectangular projector so ported tests stay byte-identical, with proj4 UTM/ENU selected for ground-mount and large sites."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_deglobalization", "label": "De-globalization of resolveRules()/resolveCatalog()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Module-level global singletons are a correctness bug in multi-tenant SaaS because geometry, pricing and sizing must vary by tenant and market; every former call site now takes context as its last parameter, and a lint grep gate keeps the strings extinct."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_three_as_math", "label": "Three-as-Math Ruling (keep three.js as CPU maths)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Porting to a neutral maths kernel during the port would violate the no-algorithm-changes rule and reopen exactly the class of drift the one-frame gate exists to prevent."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_normalizeproject", "label": "normalizeProject (normalize-on-read, Exhaustive<T> guard)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Its guarantees are load-bearing: per-item drop-with-reason, the Exhaustive<T> field-naming trick that caught the discount-erasure bug, byte-identical fingerprint preservation, and a NaN guard on weather."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_port_batches", "label": "Nine Port Batches A\u2013I with three gates each", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_golden_files", "label": "Golden-File Pinning (byte-identical snapshots)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any diff in the structure or BOM golden snapshots after the port is a port defect, not an improvement."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_not_ported", "label": "Deliberately Not Ported (store, persistence, proxies, R3F)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The freemium planLimitKw gate is deleted from the RulesContext schema entirely \u2014 plan gating is a billing concern, never a design-capacity cap, so no kW clamp exists anywhere in domain."}, {"id": "docs_05_domain_migration_purity_contract", "label": "Domain Purity Contract (enforced, not promised)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "dependency-cruiser blocks NestJS/React/fetch/storage/process.env/db/contracts imports in packages/domain; allowed deps are polygon-clipping, three (math only) and proj4."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_05_domain_migration_port_philosophy", "target": "docs_05_domain_migration_port_batches", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_05_domain_migration_domaincontext", "target": "docs_05_domain_migration_rulescontext", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_05_domain_migration_domaincontext", "target": "docs_05_domain_migration_catalogcontext", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/05-domain-migration.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_05_domain_migrati